<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for April 11.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for April 11.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following data and forecasts for gas use in the period April 9 to 11.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 9 (actual) 196 mcm, 46 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 10(forecast) 193 mcm, 45 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 11 (forecast) 202 mcm, 47 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>Apr 9 (actual) 11.7 Celsius, SNT 8.9 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 10(forecast) 11.6 Celsius, SNT 9.0 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 11 (forecast) 8.9 Celsius, SNT 9.1 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no interruption on Thursday, with none expected on Friday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5387</p>
</text>
